======= What are some considerations when performing evidence acquisitions? =======

When performing evidence collection, one key consideration is where the evidence is being collected from: bare metal, laptop, physical server, cloud VM, or VPC environment.
In a cloud/VPC environment, we may be able to collect evidence by taking a cloud snapshot/image of the VM’s attached disk volumes from the cloud account. 
This is different from bare metal collection, where we may need to physically access the disk, use forensic imaging tools, or collect from the live operating system.

We also need to consider if LVMs are being used. LVMs are logical storage areas on top of disk or partitions. So when running lsblk, one would typically see /dev/sda1,sda2, or /dev/vda1,vda2. These are partitions.
Of that partition, assuming lVMs are being used, one would see a LVM (physical volume - which its ironic because its not physical, since its on top of something logical, hence its a logical physical volume),  then carved out is volume group, 
which is the name of the volume, and then the actual logical volume. 

